# Ask, don't guess

## Ask first when

Before writing code, changing architecture, or stating product facts, ask if anything is:

- Unclear, ambiguous, or underspecified
- Missing (requirements, API shape, schema, credentials, vendor choice)
- A "probably fine" default that would lock the project in

Use short, concrete questions. Options are fine. Do not invent missing specs.

## Act without asking when

- Verified project context already answers it — use it, do not re-ask settled facts.
- You are sure — proceed.

## When docs and code conflict

Trust verified code and runtime evidence. Mark stale docs `> NEEDS VERIFICATION`, or ask which source is truth.

**Unclear → ask. Clear → build.**
